# WAIO egress allowlist -- Data Loss Prevention / Emergency Shutdown layer
# format: HOST|PORT|LABEL
#   HOST  - exact hostname/IP a worker is about to connect to (no wildcards)
#   PORT  - exact port, or "*" to allow any port on that host
#   LABEL - free-form description (documentation only)
# lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
# egress_check() in security/lib.sh denies (and trips Emergency
# Shutdown) any destination not listed here. Adding a new outbound
# destination requires an explicit line here, the same way a new
# worker requires an explicit workers/registry.conf line -- no NAME or
# destination is ever inferred or hardcoded elsewhere.
#
# This is an example/template (Public / Private Security Boundary
# Audit, Phase 29). Copy it to security/egress_allowlist.conf and fill
# in this deployment's real destinations -- see README.md's Setup
# section. The real file is gitignored: if it is missing entirely,
# egress_check() fails closed (denies everything and trips Emergency
# Shutdown), never fails open.
localhost|3000|Takomachi API gateway (RESEARCH/ANALYSIS/AI/HEALTHCHECK)
REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_RPI_HOST|22|Raspberry Pi (RPI worker)
REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_800_HOST|22|800号機 (HOST800 worker, host read from workers/800.json)
